  "description": "She has a childhood friend, Do Ryun-Nim, who habitually proposed to her when she was young… It is true that she liked the kind, pitiful, and intelligent Do Ryun-Nim, but Hazel, as an adult, had long since figured out the main point. Do Ryun-Nim is the youngest son of a duke’s family, and I am the young lady of a baron’s family in name only. So there will be no marriage in this life. I will live my life with the sole goal of admiring the physical beauty of men in public places (fighting arenas) and touching the chest of the royal family man. I returned home with that promise. “So, it’s not like this, Do Ryun-Nim… Huh?” As if to drive home the fact that you are no longer my ideal type, the moment she lightly touched Do Ryun-Nim’s weak chest. \n\n*“…Why is it like this?”\n\n“Heez, I’m sorry. Are you mad? Do you want to touch my chest?”*\n\n(Source: Ridibooks, translated)\n\n*Note: Includes one extra chapter.*",
